{"schema_version":"benchmark-q1-semantic-issue-coverage-judgment-luna5","question_id":"Q1-semantic-issue-coverage","status":"ok","judge_run_name":"luna8-api-v4-medium-mimo-v26pro-rl-max-full200-n04","prediction_set_name":"mimo-v26pro-rl-max-full200-n04","paper_id":"2602.01636","judge_input_sha256":"e04a9589495c4c525b16bea7b236a3e4245d07cefbb29d9985aa3d329e57d0d0","gold_decisions":[{"gold_issue_id":"2602.01636:I001","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2602.01636:I001:U001","2602.01636:I001:U002","2602.01636:I001:U005"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U005","ISSUE-001:U009"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns the data regularity required for residual functions, L2 norms, and equilibrated reconstruction on an H^{-1} load class. ISSUE-001 instead concerns Holder integrability of coefficient-derivative terms in a quasilinear linearisation; these are different hypotheses and failed obligations.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2602.01636:I002","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-002","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2602.01636:I002:U001","2602.01636:I002:U002","2602.01636:I002:U005","2602.01636:I002:U007"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-002:U001","ISSUE-002:U002","ISSUE-002:U007"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is the constant nullspace, compatibility, and nonuniqueness of the unrestricted CR auxiliary problem. ISSUE-002 concerns a sign in the adjoint residual flux mismatch, not solvability or boundary-face constraints of the CR problem.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2602.01636:I003","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2602.01636:I003:U001","2602.01636:I003:U002","2602.01636:I003:U003","2602.01636:I003:U004"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U005","ISSUE-001:U009"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is the invalid global L-infinity control assumption for H_0^1 in dimensions two and three and the resulting failure of the claimed C3 certificate. ISSUE-001 identifies a separate Holder-exponent restriction for coefficient derivatives, without recognizing the missing global L-infinity embedding or the unsupported C3 claim.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2602.01636:I004","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-002","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2602.01636:I004:U001","2602.01636:I004:U002","2602.01636:I004:U003","2602.01636:I004:U004","2602.01636:I004:U007"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-002:U001","ISSUE-002:U002","ISSUE-002:U003","ISSUE-002:U007","ISSUE-002:U008"],"same_causal_subject":true,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"ISSUE-002 correctly identifies the physical adjoint flux sign and the need for a plus flux mismatch, but it does not recognize the gold defect's full source/flux orientation inconsistency. Its repair explicitly leaves the element residual source unchanged, whereas the gold concern requires choosing one orientation consistently and changing the source sign when using -G.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2602.01636:I006","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"no_substantive_overlap","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2602.01636:I006:U002","2602.01636:I006:U003","2602.01636:I006:U004","2602.01636:I006:U008","2602.01636:I006:U009"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U005","ISSUE-001:U009"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns the topology and endpoint classification of the admissible rho set, including singleton and closed-interval cases and the resulting bisection qualification. Neither prediction addresses this scalar admissible-set geometry or endpoint logic.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]}],"audit":{"all_gold_ids_decided":true,"all_ranked_candidates_considered":true,"target_type_not_used_for_identity":true,"severity_not_used_for_identity":true,"prediction_reuse_requires_explicit_issue_support":true,"each_gold_credited_at_most_once":true,"combined_entries_are_self_contained_diagnoses":true,"support_limit_three_respected":true}}